.TH STOP-DAQ.SH 1 "2026-09-14" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stop-daq.sh \- stop the Mu2e DAQ for one or all partitions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stop-daq.sh
[\fB\-c\fR \fIconfig\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIpartition\fR]
[\fB\-A\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIseconds\fR]
[\fB\-y\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stop-daq.sh
shuts a partition down by sending \fBots \-k\fR into each of the tmux
windows that
.BR start-daq.sh (1)
created, waiting for \fBots\fR to exit, and then killing the session.
.PP
Windows are located by name
(\fBdaq\-\fIpartition\fB\-\fIenvironment\fR) rather than by index, so
a partition started with a different environment ordering, or with
windows added by hand, still stops correctly. A window named in the
configuration but absent from the session is reported and skipped.
.PP
After the transition requests are sent, the session is polled until no
pane is still running \fBots\fR, or until the timeout expires. A
timeout is reported as a warning and the session is killed anyway.
Use \fB\-k\fR to skip the wait entirely.
.PP
Because this stops data taking, confirmation is requested unless
\fB\-y\fR is given.
.SH OPTIONS
Configuration precedence is command line, then environment variable,
then .env file, then config file, then built-in default.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Operations YAML to read. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_CONFIG\fR.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-partition " " \fINAME\fR
Partition to stop. Environment: \fBMU2EDAQ_PARTITION\fR. Default:
\fIpartition_0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-all
Stop every partition in the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kill\-session
Kill the tmux session immediately after sending \fBots \-k\fR, without
waiting for a clean shutdown.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
How long to wait for \fBots\fR to exit. Environment:
\fBMU2EDAQ_STOP_TIMEOUT\fR. Default: \fI30\fR.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be done and change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace execution with \fBset \-x\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B STOP_DAQ_SH_OPTS
Extra options, prepended to the command line. For compatibility with
the pre-rename \fBkill_daq\fR script, \fBSTOP_DAQ_OPTS\fR and then
\fBKILL_DAQ_OPTS\fR are consulted in that order when
\fBSTOP_DAQ_SH_OPTS\fR is unset.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every targeted partition was stopped, nothing was running, or the
operator declined at the prompt.
.TP
.B 1
tmux is missing or the configuration could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
A command line option was not recognised.
.SH EXAMPLES
Stop the default partition without prompting:
.PP
.RS
.nf
stop-daq.sh -y
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stop everything, killing the sessions outright:
.PP
.RS
.nf
stop-daq.sh -A -k -y
.fi
.RE
.PP
Allow two minutes for a clean shutdown:
.PP
.RS
.nf
stop-daq.sh -z partition_0 -t 120
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-daq.sh (1),
.BR daq-status.sh (1),
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR tmux (1)
